  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="a950-7898-af00-b738" name="Polish (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #75 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The birth of Poland as a kingdom can be traced back to 966 with the ‘Baptism of Poland’ when the king, Mieszko I accepted Christianity. Early polish history was marked by a state of almost constant war with their German neighbours to the point that the first Polish king had to recognize the Emperor as his overlord. In the mid- 12th century, the army was slowly modernized, with the disappearance of the old Druzhina and professional soldiers taking the role of the mustered peasants. In the 13th century when tensions between the Teutonic knights and Poland started, the Mongol Invasion shattered the established order. The Polish army was completely restructured during the reign of Casimir the Great in the mid-14th Century, a few years before the union with the kingdom of Lithuania. War Wagons: You may have up to one War Wagon for every full 1200pts of your army. Wagon Tabor: You may have a Wagon Tabor. Defenders may exchange their bow for a crossbow (+2). Mercenaries: All these units are Unreliable. Allies: Feudal Polish may have Early German (Imperial only) or Baltic Pagans (Lithuanian) allies. Later Polish may have Later Hungarian allies.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Polish - Early Polish (966-1150)]
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Mercenaries: up to 0%
  War Wagons and Artillery: up to 0%
  Characters: Up to 25% Cavalry: Up to 50% May only take Druzhina. Infantry: At least 25% War Wagons &amp; Artillery: none Mercenaries: none Allies: none
[Polish - Feudal Polish (1150-1360)]
  Cavalry: at least 33%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Mercenaries: up to 33%
  War Wagons and Artillery: up to 0%
  Characters: Up to 25% Cavalry: At least 33% Infantry: Up to 50% War Wagons &amp; Artillery: none Mercenaries: Up to 33% Allies: up to 25%
[Polish - Medieval / Later Polish (1360-1500)]
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 33%
  Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Characters: Up to 25% Cavalry: At least 50% Infantry: Up to 33% War Wagons &amp; Artillery: May have up to one War Wagon per 1200pts, and up to one Cannon per 2400pts. Mercenaries: Up to 25% May not have Russians. Cumans may not outnumber Lithuanians. Allies: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
